From 2ab30def6a78543ee7569197c47942707fa436ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 09:55:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [DOSKUTSU] patch 0308 -- centre the thrash arm's direct
 backdrop write

Patch 0303 centred the cached backdrop and tilemap BLITS. It did not fix
the truncation, because the backdrop reaches the window by two routes and
only one of them performs a blit.

Operator report on the round-4 binary, which contains 0303: "Background
starts centered, but then as player moves becomes black on right and
bottom." Both halves are informative. "Starts centered" is new -- that is
0303 working on the cache route. "As player moves" is the handover to the
route it does not cover.

When the backdrop cache thrashes, map.cpp dispatches to the direct arm,
which calls `_render_layered_to_surface(win, r)` against the WINDOW
surface. Nothing in that function is centring-aware:

  map.cpp   SDL_FillSurfaceRect(target, NULL, clear_pixel)   whole surface
  map.cpp   } while (dx < destwd);  destwd = screenWidth * scale   logical

So it fills all 512x384 and then tiles the five parallax layers across only
the logical 320x240 at the surface origin. Against a game box at
(96,72)-(416,312) that leaves the backdrop short by exactly 96 on the right
and 72 on the bottom -- the reported geometry.

It also explains the COLOUR, which is what raises this from plausible to
confirmed. `clear_pixel` initialises to 0 and is overridden only for
backdrops 9/10/12/13/14, so on every other map the uncovered region is
filled with zero and reads as black rather than as the backdrop's sky
tone. The operator said black.

Confirmed empirically before writing this: `backdrop cache: thrashing-
detect engaged (streak=4, route=direct)` fires ~30 times per cell across
all four round-3 Mach64 cells (6C4M 30, 651M 31, 6C4I 30, 651I 31). The
direct arm is not an edge case on this card -- it engages repeatedly
through a normal reel, and camera motion is what drives the miss streak.

The fix threads a `centred` flag rather than inferring one. True only for
the window-target call; the cache-fill call passes false and keeps writing
at the cache's own origin, because `drawCachedBackdrop` is what centres
that copy on its way out and offsetting in both places would translate
twice -- the same double-apply trap 0296 documented for the dirty rects.

Two details that are load-bearing rather than tidy:

  - The clear is limited to the BOX. A full-surface fill would repaint the
    margin with clear_pixel, which is invisible while that value is zero
    and becomes a coloured frame around the picture the moment a backdrop
    sets it. It would also undo 0296's one-shot margin clear on every
    thrash frame for no benefit, since the margin can never be flushed.

  - The tile clamp is required, not decorative. SDL_BlitSurface clips to
    the destination SURFACE, not to the box, so without it the tile
    straddling the logical right edge spills into the cleared margin.
    Same for the bottom, where the last layer's height runs one row past
    the logical screen.

Checked and NOT implicated: the 0183 / SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_THRASH_FULLCOVER
path, flagged as a lead because it fixed a same-shaped backdrop-black-on-
scroll bug in v1.0.4. Its effect is to gate `bg_subregion_on` OFF, which
routes thrash frames to the full-screen `drawCachedBackdrop` rather than
the clipped variant -- i.e. to the path 0303 already centres. It carries no
320x240-shaped assumption of its own.

Native path unchanged, not merely equivalent: both offsets are zero
whenever the target is the cache, or the surface is the logical screen, or
centring is off -- and at zero the fill takes its literal pre-patch
`SDL_FillSurfaceRect(target, NULL, ...)` call and the clamp arithmetic is
skipped entirely.

Not folded into 0303 by amendment: 0303 is in the round-4 binary that ran
on hardware, and 0304-0307 sit on top of it. Rewriting a patch that a
tested binary corresponds to is how a series stops describing the thing
that was measured.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/map.cpp | 63 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 57 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/map.cpp b/src/map.cpp
index 110ca8c0..03f58833 100644
--- a/src/map.cpp
+++ b/src/map.cpp
@@ -690,7 +690,15 @@ static void _fastleft_layered_update_parscroll(Renderer *r);
 //
 // Returns true on success, false if the source backdrop is missing or
 // format-mismatched (caller falls back to legacy DrawFastLeftLayered).
-static bool _render_layered_to_surface(SDL_Surface *target, Renderer *r)
+// DOS-PORT (patch 0303 ext): `centred` is true ONLY when `target` is the
+// window surface. The thrash / direct-render arm draws straight into the
+// window, so on a centred oversized surface its output has to be placed at
+// the box like every other path. The cache-fill call passes false and keeps
+// writing at the cache's own origin, because drawCachedBackdrop is what
+// centres that copy on its way out -- offsetting here as well would apply
+// the translation twice.
+static bool _render_layered_to_surface(SDL_Surface *target, Renderer *r,
+                                       bool centred)
 {
   if (!target || !backdrop[map.backdrop]) return false;
   SDL_Surface *bg_src = backdrop[map.backdrop]->surfaceCpu();
@@ -712,7 +720,29 @@ static bool _render_layered_to_surface(SDL_Surface *target, Renderer *r)
     clear_pixel = SDL_MapSurfaceRGB(target, 170, 101, 0);
   else if (map.backdrop == 14)
     clear_pixel = SDL_MapSurfaceRGB(target, 202, 97, 97);
-  SDL_FillSurfaceRect(target, NULL, clear_pixel);
+  // DOS-PORT (patch 0303 ext): offsets are non-zero only on the window
+  // target under centring. Zero everywhere else, which keeps the cache-fill
+  // call and every native-320x240 card on the pre-patch arithmetic.
+  const int _bx = (centred && r->_dos_center_active) ? r->_dos_center_ox : 0;
+  const int _by = (centred && r->_dos_center_active) ? r->_dos_center_oy : 0;
+  const int _bw = r->screenWidth  * r->scale;
+  const int _bh = r->screenHeight * r->scale;
+
+  if (_bx == 0 && _by == 0)
+  {
+    SDL_FillSurfaceRect(target, NULL, clear_pixel);
+  }
+  else
+  {
+    // Clear the BOX, not the surface. The full-surface fill would repaint
+    // the margin with clear_pixel -- which defaults to 0 and so reads as
+    // black, indistinguishable from the margin 0296 cleared once, until a
+    // backdrop with a non-zero clear colour makes it a visible frame around
+    // the picture. It would also undo that one-shot clear on every thrash
+    // frame for no benefit, since the margin can never be flushed.
+    SDL_Rect _boxr = {_bx, _by, _bw, _bh};
+    SDL_FillSurfaceRect(target, &_boxr, clear_pixel);
+  }
 
   int layer_ys[] = {87, 122, 145, 176, 240};
   if (r->widescreen) layer_ys[4] = 272;
@@ -739,11 +769,32 @@ static bool _render_layered_to_surface(SDL_Surface *target, Renderer *r)
     dst.h = src.h;
     dst.y = y1 * r->scale;
 
+    // DOS-PORT (patch 0303 ext): translate into the box and clamp to it.
+    // The loop bound stays in LOGICAL space -- `destwd` is the logical
+    // width, so the tile sequence is unchanged and only its placement
+    // moves. The clamp is required rather than decorative: SDL_BlitSurface
+    // clips to the destination SURFACE, not to the box, so the tile
+    // straddling the logical right edge would otherwise spill into the
+    // cleared margin. Same reasoning for the bottom, where the last
+    // layer's height can run one row past the logical screen.
     int dx = x * r->scale;
     do
     {
-      dst.x = dx;
-      SDL_BlitSurface(bg_src, &src, target, &dst);
+      SDL_Rect _s = src;
+      SDL_Rect _d = dst;
+      _d.x = dx + _bx;
+      _d.y = dst.y + _by;
+
+      if (_bx != 0 || _by != 0)
+      {
+        const int _over_r = (_d.x + _d.w) - (_bx + _bw);
+        if (_over_r > 0) { _d.w -= _over_r; _s.w -= _over_r; }
+        const int _over_b = (_d.y + _d.h) - (_by + _bh);
+        if (_over_b > 0) { _d.h -= _over_b; _s.h -= _over_b; }
+      }
+
+      if (_d.w > 0 && _d.h > 0)
+        SDL_BlitSurface(bg_src, &_s, target, &_d);
       dx += sfc_w * r->scale;
     } while (dx < destwd);
     y1 = y2 + 1;
@@ -2385,7 +2436,7 @@ void map_draw_backdrop(void)
               // above (bg_src->format == win->format) so the
               // SDL_BlitSurface inner calls resolve to per-row memcpy.
               r->prepareDirectBackdropWrite();
-              if (_render_layered_to_surface(win, r))
+              if (_render_layered_to_surface(win, r, /*centred=*/true))
               {
                 r->commitDirectBackdropWrite();
                 int mapy = map.displayed_yscroll / CSFI;
@@ -2423,7 +2474,7 @@ void map_draw_backdrop(void)
               }
 
               if (g_backdrop_cache_sfc &&
-                  _render_layered_to_surface(g_backdrop_cache_sfc, r))
+                  _render_layered_to_surface(g_backdrop_cache_sfc, r, /*centred=*/false))
               {
                 g_backdrop_cache_curmap     = game.curmap;
                 g_backdrop_cache_id         = map.backdrop;
-- 
